// The modules in this repository are developed together, so building and
// testing here must use the code in the tree rather than the last published
// tag of each sibling.
//
// Without this, CI silently tested the wrong thing. blob/multipart/s3mp
// requires blob/multipart v0.1.0, and blob/multipart requires
// blob/httpblob v0.1.0, so a fix committed to httpblob was invisible to the
// multipart tests and a fix to the conformance suite was invisible to s3mp.
// Both jobs failed against code that had already been corrected in the same
// commit.
//
// This file is local to the repository. It is not consulted by anything that
// depends on these modules, so the published go.mod files still resolve
// through the proxy exactly as a consumer sees them, with no replace
// directives. Consumability is verified from outside the repo, not from here.
go 1.25.8

use (
	.
	./blob/httpblob
	./blob/multipart
	./blob/multipart/azmp
	./blob/multipart/gcsmp
	./blob/multipart/s3mp
	./blob/sftpblob
)
